      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah - this part tripped me up because most cases where we have to modify while iterating over a set, we have an ID of some sort as the PK. \n\n    for thing in things:\n        values \u003d {\u0027key\u0027: some_value}\n        update \u003d thing_table.update().where(\n            thing_table.c.id \u003d\u003d thing.id\n        ).values(values)\n        session.execute(update)\n        session.commit()\n    session.close()\n\nI wasn\u0027t sure how to do that here because the PK for the assignment table is literally every column.",
