      "writtenOn": "2017-09-08T13:53:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We have two options for handling that. \n\n1.) We can make keystone smart enough to check both columns and pick the right value. If `assignment_type` is None and `type` is not, port the value to `assignment_type`. We\u0027d have to maintain this code for a release. This will mean we have to keep the `type` column until Rocky opens. That is assuming every assignment is touched while Queens is deployed in order to move the assignment `type` to `assignment_type`.\n\n2.) Use a trigger to ensure the data from `type` is put into `assignment_type` if an update happens during a migration. This approach will allow us to drop the `type` column in contract of this migration.\n\nThis also only applies to rolling upgrades or live upgrades. If the data is migrated while keystone is offline, we don\u0027t have an issue.",
      "parentUuid": "7f287b81_38b722f8",
